<!-- SCRUM-467: TEST-LOCAL object-level access for the SCRUM-467 fixture users ONLY
     (house pattern: SCRUM442/451/464_TestObjectAccess; deliberately NOT a released PS).
     Measured 2026-11-21 in Test-Org: an Opportunity save by a fixture user runs the org's
     AfterUpdate chain OpportunityFollowupMonitorTrigger -> FollowupMonitoringHandler
     .recalculate, whose SOQL (live class line 112 and 133) reads the SCRUM-440 follow-up
     fields and the Followup_Obligation__c object. Without those grants the save dies with
     "No such column 'Followup_Required__c' on entity Opportunity" - trigger Apex runs in USER
     mode, so FLS governs its reads and writes (skill salesforce-describe-first). Hence: object
     CRUD, Read of every OTHER Opportunity custom field, Edit only on writable fields (formula
     fields stay editable=false - a trigger can never write a derived field). It names NONE of
     the seven SCRUM-467 offer fields, so AC13 keeps them inaccessible. Never assigned to a real
     user. -->
